                <pb facs="0223" n="149" xml:id="pg149"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. King.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 4, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We have telegraphic information from Mr.
                    Hale, United States consul general at Alexandria, of the arrest of John H.
                    Surratt there. In consequence of this, Admiral Goldsborough has been ordered to
                    send a war vessel thither for the purpose of bringing the prisoner here for
                    trial. It is desirable and important that St. Marie, to whom you have referred
                    in your despatches, should also be sent hither as a witness. You will
                    consequently apply for his discharge from the military service of the Pope, and,
                    if the application should be granted, you will forward him hither. The credit
                    for $—— touching the Surratt case, with which you have already been provided,
                    will, it is presumed, be enough to defray the expenses incident to the execution
                    of the, instructions, including the travelling expenses of St. Marie.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rufus King,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
